ions is that when you sit down  the couch is basically just looking at  the back of the desk which is not a  great View  so I just don't see this couch being  used he also said he rarely has people  over and he usually just uses the couch  for doing those interviews honestly I  feel like it's a little bit of a waste  of space so what if instead of having an  entire couch we just had  two armchairs that way the view is not  towards the living room but he can  actually look out  also when he's doing interviews he can  sit here the guests can be sitting here  and they can have the camera facing this  way  if you want to take a break from his  computer and go read on his iPad or go  read a book or something he can use this  as a lounging area so this area is more  for Focus work and this area can be more  for diffuse work and your creativity  actually benefits a lot from going back  and forth so I really like this idea of  having the arm chairs here so that kind  of leaves us with two options this one  or  this one this option you could film with  this wall as the backdrop it would be a  different kind of office scene but it  could definitely work and this way he  can have his entire area over here for  doing yoga or physio so I'm gonna try to  develop  these two options this one and this one  a little bit more in detail  so this is the elevation facing the wall  I'll bring this into more folio trace  and start sketching on top of that using  their perspective guides which is super  helpful for quickly and accurately  sketching out ideas I want to do like an  upper level of storage where he can keep  things like he rarely needs or things  that he wants to keep on display  and I think this also kind of helps to  Define this area and that's kind of what  I want to do I want to Define this  entire zone for his creative work where  he can kind of spread out you know throw  his ideas around and kind of get messy  so I've wrapped this entire area with  cork board so you can p